2026-11-12T07:46:38.9878266Z --- SCRIPT-DUMP-BUILD_TOP-HEAD ---
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9879488Z """Dataset "top": several current top-of-ladder strategies as teachers, each on its own style row, whole games.
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9881145Z Why: one teacher's games are few for a 3M-parameter net (Master3s: ~120 games); the other strong players' games teach
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9882770Z the trunk the same board situations (trees under contest, crowded bases, fights for cargo) from several hands, while
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9884688Z the style row keeps whose decisions are whose.
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9885861Z   python3 build_top.py OUT_DIR REPLAY_DIR [REPLAY_DIR ...]    then    python3 set_uw.py OUT_DIR 1 1 1
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9887404Z Teachers: the default set (J1, five teachers, rows 2-6), or CNET2_TOP=J2 (eight teachers, all rows), or an explicit
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9888992Z CNET2_TOP_TEACHERS="name@row,name@row,..." (rows 0-7; names exactly as on the leaderboard).
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9890264Z Master3s stays on row 2 in every set -- the row the Echo packs play.
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9891582Z Only ladder replays (public games) -- never games generated locally with someone's public source."""
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9892727Z import os
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9893610Z import sys
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9894221Z import cnet2_feat as F
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9894722Z 
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9895083Z SETS = {
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9896111Z     "J1": {2: "claude-AlphaCarbon-Master3s", 3: "RyanX-AIPowercore-M6", 4: "stephen-K4TacSearch-v1",
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9897519Z            5: "AgyCarbon-P2C-Godslayer-CV", 6: "claude-AlphaCarbon-Master2s"},
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9898869Z     "J2": {2: "claude-AlphaCarbon-Master3s", 3: "RyanX-AIPowercore-M6", 4: "stephen-K4TacSearch-v1",
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9900162Z            5: "AgyCarbon-P2C-Godslayer-CV", 6: "claude-AlphaCarbon-Master2s",
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9901298Z            0: "Carago-V2", 1: "RyanX-AIPowercore-M2", 7: "Fable5.2-Max-V3"},
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9902141Z }
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9902725Z spec = os.environ.get("CNET2_TOP_TEACHERS")
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9903737Z if spec:
2026-11-12T07:46:38.9904522Z     rows = {int(r): n for n, r in (item.rsplit("@", 1) for item in spec.split(",") if item)}
